module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.caret_symbol_has_no_lowered_form

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data caret_symbol_has_no_lowered_form: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "caret_symbol_has_no_lowered_form" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "no lowered form for a caret symbol `^sym` in v2 body lowering: `v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_caret_symbol_expr` writes it as seq(`^`, ident), and no reader in `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` lowers that sequence. As an operator operand (`x == ^sym`) it refuses as `body_lowering_reason_operator_operand_unread`, located at the operand; on the bottom-up value route `body_lower_primary_expr` answers it with `body_lower_pattern_first_atom_optional`, the `^` token, so the symbol it names is lost there without a diagnostic.",
    "SPECIMENS AND PINNED LOCUS: `dag/test/claim/long/dag_arrow_lambda_witness_test.dag` and `src/v2/test/claim/manual/body_lowering_projection_call_test.dag`, each refusing `operator_operand_unread` at a `dag_surface_primary_expr` whose atoms are `dag_token_caret dag_token_ident`.",
    "EXPOSED, NOT INTRODUCED: the parent of gunbc#12145 (2de78893dfe) accepted this shape only by SILENT NARROWING -- the operand reader answered a sequence with its left element -- so the refusal on main after gunbc#12173 is a pre-existing defect made visible, not a new regression. Found by the XL-2 three-baseline identity census on gunbc#12194 (321 paths: 18 refusing at 2de78893dfe, 167 at ada85b9452, 101 after gunbc#12173).",
    "THE BELOW-FLOOR INSTANCE, OBSERVED ON main b1b7aea9aa7: `v2.std.compilers.target_model` `ordering_predicate_from_wire_symbol` -- `if id == ^ordering_predicate_is_less {..} else if id == ^ordering_predicate_is_less_or_equal {..}` -- normalizes ACCEPTED, and its normalized tree carries `^dag_token_caret` and neither `^ordering_predicate_is_less` nor `^ordering_predicate_is_less_or_equal`: both conditions lowered to `id == ^`, so two different caret symbols became one node. Bare-operand bodies (`v2.std.grammar` `formal_binding_is_free_name_slot`, `formal_binding_is_lexeme_stamp_slot`; `v2.std.compilers.target_model` `target_model_bundle_core_keep_edge`) still refuse at normalize as `operator_operand_unread`. Measured by a seed-interpreted probe of tokenize -> parse -> normalize (branch probe/snappy-swift-136-mq1-caret @ 2349f5371d4). `v2.compiler.reference_conservation` did not report the drop (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode reference_conservation_population_omits_class_stamped_terminals).",
    "REFUSED, ONE CAUSE, AT THE CARET (MQ-1 PR-1): `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_primary_expr`'s first-atom fallback refuses the caret shape as `body_lowering_reason_caret_symbol_not_lowered`, anchored at the `^` token, so the ten silently-dropping value positions and the bare operand refuse with one cause, pinned by `v2.test.claim.body_lowering.caret_symbol_value_refusal`. The rung on every route is now mitigated (a located refusal); the symbol-literal lowering is the climb.",
    "HANDED TO THE MQ-1 SYMBOL-LITERAL SLICE, NOT BUILT IN XL-2 (2026-09-29, sharp-carp-336, ruled by quiet-seal-543). For XL-2 the located refusal is sufficient: a caret is a literal, not a reference the namespace cut can break. Three findings bound the climb. (1) THE NAME TEXT IS NOT IN THE TREE, BY DESIGN: `v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_caret_symbol_expr` class-stamps the name (`dag_grammar_ident_or_type_decl_modifier_generic_ident_identity`), so every caret literal publishes the generic `^dag_token_ident`. `v2.lens.identity_captured_navigation.analyze` `node_source_symbol_note` states that as a universal property and recovers the text out of band through the span index. The lowering must first stamp that site with its lexeme and rewrite that note. (2) THE TARGET IS THE EXISTING AUTHORITY: `std.syntax` `LitSymbol`, as `v2.workflow.compile_door_cause_ownership`'s caret row states; a new literal form beside it would be a second authority. (3) TYPING IT `Symbol` IS STEP (a) OF `gunbc.symbol_identity_census` `symbol_nominality_next_rung_trigger`, not a separate decision; v2 infer also has no `Symbol` or `String` row in `dag_binding_denotation`, so a declared `-> Symbol` is not checked today. CORRECTION TO THE RECEIPTS ABOVE, MEASURED ON MAIN 88436e585c3: a caret in value position, as a statement-let value and as an operator operand refuses `body_lowering_reason_caret_symbol_not_lowered`, but as the value of an `in`-form let (`let x = ^s in b`) it was ACCEPTED with the caret dropped, because `body_lower_try_let_in_from_captured` reads that value through `body_lower_arm_operand_resolved_optional`. That instance belongs to the first-match readers' consolidation (XL-2 PR-2, bright-boar-848), which reads the let-in value through the one value reader and carries it as a discriminating control.",
    "LOWERED, AND THE CLASS IS CLOSED AT ITS CEILING (MQ-1 PR-2): `v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_caret_symbol_expr` lexeme-stamps the name (`dag_grammar_ident_or_type_decl_modifier_name`), and `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_caret_symbol_literal_optional` lowers seq(`^`, name) to `dag_symbol_literal_node` -- the caret atom carrying the name terminal, occurrence kept, as its one named payload (std.syntax LitSymbol, std.literal_elaboration KernelSymbolLiteral). `v2.compiler.resolve` `resolve_atom` returns it whole without lookup (`dag_symbol_literal_name_optional`). PR-1's refusal and its `v2.workflow.compile_door_cause_ownership` row are retired. Every value position, the bare operand and the disjunction lower with their exact payloads in order (`v2.test.claim.body_lowering.caret_symbol_value_lowering`); an operand naming undeclared symbols resolves (`v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal` `a_caret_symbol_operand_resolves_without_lookup`). Its TYPE is derived in v2 infer: v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_canonical_literal_from_node reads it as DagCanonicalSymbolLiteral, which v2.compiler.infer infer_literal_type_binding types as v2.std.node Symbol through the binding join to v2.std.node symbol_type_node. `let y: Int = ^s` refuses at the annotation, and `let y: Symbol = ^s` is admitted with no frontier at the literal (v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation bla_symbol_literal_ascribed_int_refuses_at_the_annotation, bla_symbol_literal_ascribed_symbol_is_admitted_and_derived). gunbc.symbol_identity_census symbol_nominality_next_rung_trigger (a) stays open: it names the SOURCE checker, v1.compiler.types, which still types LitSymbol as the kernel string_type.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigated (a located refusal) on the operator route; below the floor on the value route. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a caret symbol lowers to a symbol-literal value the resolver does not read as a reference, or refuses. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: v2 body lowering has a lowered form for a caret symbol on every route, distinct from a reference, so no route answers it with its `^` token and no route refuses it as unread. REACHED by MQ-1 PR-2; the discriminating controls stay enrolled (DESIGN 4b(4)).",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal", decl_name: "a_caret_symbol_operand_resolves_without_lookup", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_lowering.caret_symbol_value_lowering", decl_name: "a_caret_symbol_if_condition_pair_lowers_to_two_different_payloads", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
